Test that the rounding scheme for multiplication of money by decimal is the
same in Z3 and OCaml.

```catala
declaration scope A:
    input x content money
    output o content integer

scope A:
    exception definition o under condition (x = $1 * -0.015)
        consequence equals 0
    exception definition o under condition (x = $1 * -0.011 and x = $1 * -0.005)
        consequence equals 1
    exception definition o under condition (x = $1 * -0.001
                                            and x = $1 * -0.000
                                            and x = $1 * 0.001)
        consequence equals 2
    exception definition o under condition (x = $1 * 0.005 and x = $1 * 0.011)
        consequence equals 3
    exception definition o under condition (x = $1 * 0.015)
        consequence equals 4

    definition o equals -1
```

```catala-test-cli
$ catala Concolic --conc-optim=incremental -s A
┌─[RESULT]─ Concolic execution ─
│ Executed 6 tests:
│        Inputs │ Outputs
│ ───────── Test #1 ─────
│ x_in = ¤0.00  │ o = 2
│ ───────── Test #2 ─────
│ x_in = ¤0.02  │ o = 4
│ ───────── Test #3 ─────
│ x_in = ¤0.03  │ o = -1
│ ───────── Test #4 ─────
│ x_in = ¤0.01  │ o = 3
│ ───────── Test #5 ─────
│ x_in = ¤-0.01 │ o = 1
│ ───────── Test #6 ─────
│ x_in = ¤-0.02 │ o = 0
└─
```

